A self-signed RSA-2048 certificate: SAN, basicConstraints, keyUsage, extendedKeyUsage.
The key is fresh on every run, so the modulus, the signature and anything derived from them differ
after a regeneration; every field src/main.rs asserts is fixed by the command below.

openssl req -x509 -newkey rsa:2048 -keyout /dev/null -noenc -sha256 \
  -not_before 20260101000000Z -not_after 20360101000000Z \
  -set_serial 0x0102030405060708 \
  -subj "/C=US/ST=California/L=San Francisco/O=neant/OU=crypto/CN=selfsigned.neant.test" \
  -addext "subjectAltName=DNS:selfsigned.neant.test,DNS:alt.neant.test,IP:127.0.0.1" \
  -addext "basicConstraints=critical,CA:TRUE,pathlen:2" \
  -addext "keyUsage=critical,digitalSignature,keyCertSign,cRLSign" \
  -addext "extendedKeyUsage=serverAuth,clientAuth" \
  -out tests/data/selfsigned-rsa.pem

